                                                "sense_id": "c43fb0bd-837d-37f7-972e-eb778d24c6df",
                                                "text": "A modern glass edifice nearby houses the headquarters of the illustrious Rothschild banking family. It was the Rothschilds who in the 1830s arranged that recently paid-off £20 million loan to the British government to reimburse slaveowners after the trade ended – said to be equivalent to some £300 billion in today’s money."
